<article>
	<h1><span>Shopping Cart: Software Downloads</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#column-headers">Column Headers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#list-filters">List Filters</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
		<li><a href="#sub-menu">Sub-menu Links</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This screen lists software downloads made through the shopping cart, one row per download.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="column-headers">
		<h2><span>Column Headers</span></h2>

		<p>Click the <strong>Product</strong>, <strong>Downloaded by</strong>, <strong>Downloaded</strong> or
			<strong>Status</strong> heading to sort the list by that column. Click it again to reverse the order.</p>

		<dl>
			<dt>Checkbox</dt>
			<dd>Check this box to select one or more items. To select all items, check the box in the column heading.
				After one or more boxes are checked, click a toolbar button to take an action on the selected item or
				items.</dd>

			<dt>Product</dt>
			<dd>The product name, with its SKU on the line below. Click the product name to list only downloads of
				that product, or the SKU to list only downloads of that SKU. <em>Product n/a</em> or <em>n/a</em> is
				shown when the product or SKU no longer exists.</dd>

			<dt>Downloaded by</dt>
			<dd>The name and username of the member who downloaded. Click it to list only that member's downloads.
				<em>(unknown)</em> is shown when the download has no member.</dd>

			<dt>User Info</dt>
			<dd>The user details recorded with the download, separated by commas.</dd>

			<dt>EULA</dt>
			<dd>Shows <em>EULA accepted</em> when the download recorded that the end user licence agreement was
				accepted.</dd>

			<dt>Downloaded</dt>
			<dd>The date and time of the download.</dd>

			<dt>IP</dt>
			<dd>The IP address the download came from.</dd>

			<dt>Status</dt>
			<dd><strong>Active</strong> or <strong>Inactive</strong>. Users who may change the state of items can
				click the status to switch it.</dd>
		</dl>

		<p>When the list is limited to one member, product or SKU, a row above the headings names it
			(<em>Orders for</em> or <em>Orders of</em>) with a <strong>Clear</strong> button.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="list-filters">
		<h2><span>List Filters</span></h2>

		<dl>
			<dt>Search</dt>
			<dd>Lists only downloads whose product name, SKU, member name or username contains the text.</dd>

			<dt>SKU</dt>
			<dd>Shown only when the list is limited to one SKU. Choose <strong>All SKUs</strong> to remove that
				limit.</dd>

			<dt>From &mdash; To</dt>
			<dd>Lists only downloads made between these dates. The default is from one month ago to today.</dd>

			<dt>Update</dt>
			<dd>Applies the filters.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Options</dt>
			<dd>Opens the Options window where settings such as default parameters or permissions can be edited.
				Shown only to users who may configure the component.</dd>

			<dt>Publish</dt>
			<dd>Shown only to users who may change the state of items. This screen has no publish action, so the
				list reloads unchanged. To make a download active, click its <strong>Status</strong>.</dd>

			<dt>Unpublish</dt>
			<dd>Shown only to users who may change the state of items. This screen has no unpublish action, so the
				list reloads unchanged. To make a download inactive, click its <strong>Status</strong>.</dd>

			<dt>Download CSV</dt>
			<dd>Downloads a CSV file of every download matching the current search, dates, SKU, member and product
				filters. Its columns are Downloaded, Product, SKU, User, Username, User ID, User Details, EULA, IP
				and Status.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="sub-menu">
		<h2><span>Sub-menu Links</span></h2>
		<p>At the top left, you will see sub-menu options. The links are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Software Downloads (this page)</dt>
			<dt>Orders</dt>
		</dl>
		<p>Below them, a second row of links chooses the report:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>All downloads (this page)</dt>
			<dt>Downloads by SKU</dt>
		</dl>
	</section>
</article>
